# SABOTAGE: P11 (phase6-punchlist) — the CSAT resolved-transition detection is gutted:
# the `changing_attribute?(:status)` conjunct is dropped and `previous_status !=
# :resolved` is neutered to a tautology (`!= :__sabotage_never__`, keeping
# `previous_status/1` referenced so this is a GENUINE behavior mutant, not a compile
# error). The survey now fires on ANY write that leaves `:status` == `:resolved` — a
# re-save / unrelated edit of an already-resolved ticket re-mints + re-dispatches a
# duplicate CSAT survey.
#
# HONEST NOTE (see gate report): Ash ELIDES same-value force-changes, so on the
# force_change_attribute(:status,:resolved) path `changing_attribute?` is already FALSE —
# which means the `changing_attribute?` and `previous_status != :resolved` conjuncts are
# mutually REDUNDANT for the same-value case and neither can be pinned ALONE (a
# single-conjunct drop is vacuous). This sabotage therefore removes the transition
# detection AS A WHOLE, which is the non-vacuous, load-bearing property. Flips BOTH the
# force_change-direct test and the normal resolved->resolved test. Reverts byte-exact.
# APP: samen_web
# TEST_FILES: test/samen/web/support_csat_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: P11 FORCE-CHANGE DIRECT: an already-resolved ticket force_change'd back to :resolved does NOT re-mint a CSAT token
# MUST_FAIL: a ticket already resolved touched again (resolved -> resolved) does not re-mint a survey
diff --git a/samen_core/lib/samen/scopes/support/csat_survey_dispatch.ex b/samen_core/lib/samen/scopes/support/csat_survey_dispatch.ex
--- a/samen_core/lib/samen/scopes/support/csat_survey_dispatch.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/samen/scopes/support/csat_survey_dispatch.ex
@@ -69,9 +69,8 @@ defmodule Samen.Scopes.Support.CsatSurveyDispatch do
   # happens to re-submit the same status) fires nothing, matching
   # `Samen.Notifications.StatusChange`'s exact discipline.
   defp transitioning_to_resolved?(changeset) do
-    Ash.Changeset.changing_attribute?(changeset, :status) and
-      Ash.Changeset.get_attribute(changeset, :status) == :resolved and
-      previous_status(changeset) != :resolved
+    Ash.Changeset.get_attribute(changeset, :status) == :resolved and
+      previous_status(changeset) != :__sabotage_never__
   end
 
   defp previous_status(%{data: %{status: status}}), do: status
